---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Authority is recognised" currentPath="/manifesto/foundations/authority">

  <article class="principle-document">
    <header class="principle-header">
      <div class="principle-meta">
        <span>I.2</span>
        <span>E01-P02</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Authority is recognised</h1>
      <p class="abstract">Authority emerges through coherence held over time, not assertion or display.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="principle-content">
      <h2>Statement</h2>
      <p>Authority is not claimed.</p>
      <p>It is recognised when a system no longer needs to explain itself.</p>

      <h2>Context</h2>
      <p>Systems that assert authority undermine it. True authority accumulates through consistent behavior — through maintaining coherence even when pressure exists to deviate.</p>
      <p>This is why promotional language weakens credibility. The system that must convince you of its value demonstrates uncertainty about that value.</p>

      <h2>Application</h2>
      <p>Authority manifests through predictability. Users learn they can depend on the system to behave consistently. This dependability becomes the foundation of trust, which is how authority is actually conferred.</p>

      <h2>Citation</h2>
      <p class="citation-text">This principle may be cited as: <strong>I.2 (Authority)</strong> or by plate reference <strong>E01-P02</strong>.</p>
    </section>
  </article>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .principle-document {
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .principle-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(42, 42, 37, 0.15);
  }

  .principle-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-nav);
    font-size: 0.55rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.45;
  }

  .principle-header h1 {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .abstract {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    font-style: italic;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .principle-content h2 {
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-nav);
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .principle-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
  }

  .citation-text {
    font-family: var(--font-nav);
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    font-style: normal;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .citation-text strong {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
    opacity: 1;
  }
</style>